---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="How to request your Discord data package (2026 guide) · Unpacked"
  description="Step-by-step on desktop and mobile: request your data package from Discord, how long it takes (up to 30 days), what's inside the ZIP, and which sections you need for playtime, streaming and voice stats."
>
  <article class="wrap prose">
    <h1>How to request your Discord data package</h1>
    <p class="muted">
      Discord will send you a copy of the data it has on your account. It's a ZIP file with your account details,
      messages, servers and a log of what you've done in the app. That log is where playtime, Go Live and voice time
      come from.
    </p>

    <h2>Before you start</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Your account needs a <strong>verified email address</strong>.</li>
      <li>
        The download link goes to the email on your account <em>when you make the request</em>. Changing your email
        afterwards won't redirect it.
      </li>
      <li>You can only have one request open at a time.</li>
      <li>Disabling or deleting your account before the link arrives cancels the request.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>1. Request it in Discord</h2>
    <h3>On a computer (desktop app or browser)</h3>
    <ol>
      <li>Click the <strong>gear</strong> in the lower-left corner to open User Settings.</li>
      <li>Open <strong>Data &amp; Privacy</strong>.</li>
      <li>Under <strong>Request your data</strong>, click <strong>Request Data</strong>.</li>
      <li>
        Choose what to include. For the stats on this site, include at least <strong>Account</strong> and
        <strong>Activity</strong>. Messages and Servers add server and channel names.
      </li>
      <li>Submit the request.</li>
    </ol>
    <h3>On your phone</h3>
    <ol>
      <li>Tap your <strong>avatar</strong> in the lower-right corner, then the <strong>gear</strong> in the upper-right.</li>
      <li>Tap <strong>Data &amp; Privacy</strong>.</li>
      <li>Under <strong>Request your data</strong>, tap <strong>Request all of my data</strong> and confirm.</li>
    </ol>
    <p class="muted">
      The phone app always requests everything; picking sections only works on a computer. Either is fine for this site.
      Discord's own steps, with screenshots:
      <a href="https://support.discord.com/hc/en-us/articles/360004027692-Requesting-a-Copy-of-your-Data" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Requesting a Copy of your Data</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Wait for the email</h2>
    <p>
      Discord emails a download link when the package is ready. Discord says this can take <strong>up to 30 days</strong>,
      though it's often much quicker. The link expires after a while, so download the ZIP when it arrives.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Open it here</h2>
    <p>
      Don't extract the ZIP. Go to <a href="/stats/">Open your package</a> and drop <code>package.zip</code> onto the
      page. It's read in your browser and never uploaded.
    </p>

    <h2>What's inside the package</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Account:</strong> your profile, connections, badges, and lifetime playtime per game.</li>
      <li><strong>Activity:</strong> large event logs (often several GB unzipped) with streams, calls and app usage.</li>
      <li><strong>Messages:</strong> your messages, one folder per channel or DM.</li>
      <li><strong>Servers:</strong> the servers you're in.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="muted">
      Discord describes every file in
      <a href="https://support.discord.com/hc/en-us/articles/360004957991-Your-Discord-Data-Package" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Your Discord Data Package</a>.
    </p>
    <p class="muted">
      Folder names are in the language your Discord is set to (for example <code>Compte/</code> in French). That's
      fine: the stats page finds files by what's in them.
    </p>

    <h2>Why some stats might be missing</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        If <strong>"Use data to improve Discord"</strong> was turned off in Data &amp; Privacy, Discord didn't log some
        activity during that time, so there will be gaps.
      </li>
      <li>If you left out the Activity section, streaming and voice stats can't be shown.</li>
    </ul>

    <p><a class="button" href="/stats/">Open your package</a></p>
  </article>
</Base>
